          "text": "Dear Colleague,\n\nHistory of Present Illness:\nThe patient has focal epilepsy with focal impaired-awareness seizures. Seizure onset was at age 37. The epilepsy has a genetic etiology due to an SCN1A c.5734C>T variant. Seizures are drug responsive.\n\nCurrent Antiseizure Medications:\n- Zonisamide\n- Perampanel\n\nSeizure Burden:\nApproximately one seizure per year.\n\nAssessment:\nDrug-responsive focal epilepsy characterized by focal impaired-awareness seizures, with onset at age 37 and a genetic etiology associated with the SCN1A c.5734C>T variant.\n\nPlan:\n- Continue current zonisamide and perampanel.\n- Continue monitoring seizure frequency.\n\nSincerely,\nEpilepsy Clinic",
